      "title": "Duplicate permission allowlist in validation logic",
      "description": "In validate_capability_request, the permissions validation branch constructs a local hardcoded set {\"cache.read\", \"cache.write\", \"local.generate\"} (line 239) instead of reusing PERMISSION_REGISTRY. This creates a maintenance risk where registry changes (e.g. adding/removing a permission) could cause semantic validation to diverge from get_granted_permissions and from the schema enum, weakening consistency of validation.",
      "reproduction": "Edit PERMISSION_REGISTRY to include a new permission name (conceptually), then pass a request containing that permission in the permissions array. validate_capability_request would not use the modified registry in that branch (uses local set) while get_granted_permissions validates against PERMISSION_REGISTRY. Concrete input: request with permissions=['cache.read','new.perm'] and PERMISSION_REGISTRY containing 'new.perm' -> semantic branch checks against local set and may behave inconsistently with other code paths."
